// spirv — the shaders, compiled, as the words Vulkan takes.
//
// The SPIR-V is committed so that a program using smalt builds with the Axle compiler
// and nothing else. Each module is `shaders/<name>` compiled and validated by glslang —
//
//     glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.0 --spirv-val -I shaders shaders/<name>
//
// — and its words written here eight to a line, as signed decimals: SPIR-V words use
// all 32 bits (the float constant -1.0 is 0xBF800000), and an Axle array literal takes
// its element type from its values, so one word past i32's range would retype the
// table. A shader edited and not recompiled into this file is a GPU running
// yesterday's lighting: `doc/GPU.md` ("Changing a shader") lists what to redo, and
// `GpuCheck::shaders` checks each module's header and size.
//
// Functions returning a table rather than constants: a top-level initialiser
// must be a literal (E0720), and `VkShaderModuleCreateInfo` wants an address
// the caller holds for the length of the call.
//
// fmt: skip — `axle fmt` puts every word of a table on a line of its own.

/** The compiled shader modules. */
pub(crate) class Spirv {
